  "brief": "<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Market Overview</h2>\n\nFutures pointing lower across the board with SPY down 0.67% at $733.73 as dollar strength and Iran war fallout weigh on risk assets. VIX climbing to 27.58 signals defensive positioning ahead of multiple Fed speakers and mortgage data. Small caps getting hit hardest with IWM down over 1%.\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> What to Watch</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Fed speakers Paulson (12:00) and Barr (14:15)</strong> - Rate hike rhetoric could accelerate dollar rally and pressure equities further</li>\n<li><strong>MBA Mortgage Applications (11:00)</strong> - Critical housing demand gauge with rates at multi-year highs</li>\n<li><strong>EIA Crude Imports (14:30)</strong> - Iran war disruption impact on supply chains becoming clearer</li>\n<li><strong>Nvidia momentum</strong> - Reuters highlighting NVDA as the go-to play during broader market weakness</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-red\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚠ Bear Case</div>Dollar at 6-week highs with more Fed hawkishness coming. Materials getting crushed (-2.35%) suggests recession fears building. War premium expanding across multiple fronts.</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Sector Rotation</h2>\n\nClear flight to defensive sectors with Healthcare (+1.10%) and Energy (+1.17%) leading as Iran conflict drives oil prices and safe-haven flows. Financials getting slammed (-1.24%) on rate curve concerns while Materials (-2.35%) signal industrial demand destruction. Classic late-cycle rotation pattern emerging.\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-amber\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚡ Key Driver</div>Dollar strength is the macro story - crushing commodities, pressuring multinationals, and signaling Fed isn't done. Watch DXY breaking above 105 for acceleration.</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Levels That Matter</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SPY $730</strong> - Key support from April lows, break opens door to $715</li>\n<li><strong>VIX $30</strong> - Panic threshold that could trigger forced covering</li>\n<li><strong>XLF $38.50</strong> - Financials support level, break confirms banking sector weakness</li>\n<li><strong>Oil $85</strong> - Iran war premium fully priced above this level</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr>\n<p><em>Not a prediction. A preparation. Make your plan before the bell.</em></p>"
